    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d18">

                <pb facs="0105" n="939" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg939"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/476</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-09T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 9, 1918, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6207. Following for Sheldon from War Trade Board:</p>
                <p>Your cable of December 29 through Department, No. 8098, also your cable through
                    Department of January 7, No. 8170, relating to alteration of embargo policy in
                    respect of nonessentials. British Embassy here have no information whatsoever
                    with regard to this suggestion and, until they hear from Foreign Office and we
                    have conferred with them, cannot answer definitely. At present we do not favor
                    the proposal, and in any event, if there is to be a relaxation upon the strict
                    embargo, we think there are several commodities which should be eliminated from
                    the list proposed, such as salvarsan, novocain, and others.</p>
                <p>Referring yours of January 7,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d18-f1"/> we will send
                    Mitchell as your assistant in connection with food import and export
                    questions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
